# retroforge: enable the gamescope session on release — retroforge-session.service logs the session user
# straight into the shell (it replaces a display manager). /etc/machine-id is empty on a fresh image
# so systemd runs preset-all on first boot, where the stock 99-default.preset is "disable *"; this
# higher-priority preset (60 < 99) keeps it enabled. The build-time display-manager.service and
# graphical.target.wants symlinks ship alongside as a fallback (cf. seatd's 60-retroforge-seatd), and
# the overlay points default.target at graphical.target, so the device boots straight into the shell.
enable retroforge-session.service
